## Rows skipped

- A21, the ZWSP half of B28, and the verdict lines on U+200B in 003, 005, 006, 008, 009, 013 and 015, including the four `**​**` lines in 005.
  Reason: zero-width counts already match the Korean source. Deleting them fails `blocks` (ZWSP parity). Instances removed: 0. Q16–Q20 were not promoted to `##` headings: heading levels must match the source. Adding headings fails `headings`.
- B52 (outline 7 → 6 and 8 → 7).
  Reason: the English source has the same skip, and ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids changing numbers. Renumbering would make the Italian outline diverge from the source. Instances changed: 0.
- B25, the bare digit 1 in “1 lampeggio”, “1 omissione”, “1 camion piccolo”, and “1 o 2 amministratori”.
  Reason: the Italian lexicon parses “un anno” and “quattro”/“dieci”, but not bare “uno”/“una”. “un solo lampeggio” / “un camion” / “uno o due” would drop those digits and fail `numbers`. The digit stays. See applied note for the wording that did change around them.

